<urn:atm:triage:finding/AG13-FIND-B4-ENTRY-GATE-SEQUENCING>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AG13-FIND-B4-ENTRY-GATE-SEQUENCING" ;
  triage:title "Entry-gate sequencing violation compounds two levels deep (AG.11 -> AG.12 -> AG.13)" ;
  triage:description "docs/plans/phase-AG/sprint-AG13.md's own Entry Gate section (line ~81-83) states \"AG.12 localhost remote-target closure is complete.\" This is false: docs/plans/phase-AG/readiness.md lines 37-39 list AG.11 as PASS but AG.12 and AG.13 both still PENDING/TBD; readiness.md lines 64-68 gate criteria explicitly state \"AG.12 does not begin until AG.11 lands\" / \"AG.13 does not begin until AG.12 lands\" -- both violated, since AG.13 work has proceeded while both AG.11 and AG.12 remain unlanded (both FAILED their own QA-1 rounds). This is the same ARCH-003/ARCH-004 pattern as AG.12 building ahead of AG.11, now recurring one level deeper." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-AG" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "file_only" ;
  triage:category "process" ;
  triage:severity "blocking" ;
  triage:status "open" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-07-18T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AG13-FIND-B4-ENTRY-GATE-SEQUENCING/sprint-AG13/1> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AG13-FIND-B4-ENTRY-GATE-SEQUENCING/readiness/1> ;
  triage:openOn <urn:atm:triage:worktree/pAG-s13/1791f5ab> ;
  triage:promoteTo <urn:atm:triage:worktree/pAG-s13/1791f5ab> ;
  triage:notes "Process/documentation-accuracy issue. Entry Gate in sprint-AG13.md falsely claims AG.12 closure is complete, but readiness.md explicitly gates both AG.12 and AG.13 pending AG.11 landing. Both AG.11 and AG.12 remain unlanded with FAILED QA-1 verdicts. This compounds the ARCH-003/ARCH-004 pattern from AG.12 (building ahead of AG.11) one level deeper (AG.13 building ahead of AG.12, which itself never landed ahead of AG.11). Team-lead should consider whether this warrants attention independent of any held-findings convention. This is a blocking process violation that undermines plan integrity across three consecutive phases. STILL OPEN at AG13-QA-3 (commit 1791f5ab): AG13-FIX-1 Group 2 corrected the sprint-AG13.md Entry Gate wording, but readiness.md was never touched -- as of this recheck, readiness.md line 37 shows AG.11 as PASS, but line 38 still shows AG.12 as PENDING/TBD ('localhost full-function same-host remote-target proof not yet executed') and line 39 still shows AG.13 as PENDING/TBD ('self-IP full-function same-host proof not yet executed'), despite AG.13 now being 3 QA rounds deep with real code landed (commits 6d2afb4c, 8ce2f9ea, 1791f5ab). The gate criteria at lines 64-65 ('AG.12 does not begin until AG.11 lands' / 'AG.13 does not begin until AG.12 lands') remain violated in the tracked readiness state itself -- this is a live process-gate violation, not merely a stale wording issue, since readiness.md is the authoritative gate record and it has never been updated on this branch." .

